Feature: Mask last 4 digits of invoice_number in the d_product_revenue_clone table

  Background:
    Given the d_product_revenue table exists in the database
    And the d_product_revenue_clone table is dropped if it exists
    And a replica of the d_product_revenue is created as d_product_revenue_clone

  Scenario: Successfully mask the last 4 digits of the invoice_number
    Given the invoice_number column contains numeric values
    When the PySpark logic is executed
    Then the last four digits of each invoice_number should be masked with '****'
    And the masked invoice_number is saved in the d_product_revenue_clone table

  Scenario: Attempt to mask with invalid data type in invoice_number column
    Given the invoice_number column contains non-numeric values
    When the PySpark logic is executed
    Then an error message is displayed "Invalid data type in invoice_number column"
    And no changes should be made to the d_product_revenue_clone table

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven tests for masking invoice_number
    Given the invoice_number column contains the value <original_value>
    When the PySpark logic is executed
    Then the stored invoice_number should be <masked_value>

    Examples:
      | original_value | masked_value |
      | 1234234534     | 123423****   |
      | 5678123412     | 567812****   |
      | 9876543210     | 987654****   |

  Scenario: No modification if d_product_revenue_clone is empty
    Given the d_product_revenue_clone table is empty
    When the PySpark logic is executed
    Then no changes should be made and table remains empty

  Scenario: Verify error message for restricted access
    Given insufficient permissions for modifying the d_product_revenue_clone table
    When the PySpark logic is executed
    Then an error message is displayed "Access denied to d_product_revenue_clone table"
    And no changes should be made to the table
